  "review_notes": "Full master and all three sheet versions inspected. v1/v2 rejected because they simplified the wooden yoke into a collar. v3 selected: distinct thick wood posts and transverse crossbeam frame the skull in every pose. Four bone legs, long horizontal spine, swept-back armor retained. Twenty actual connected silhouettes; rows idle/walk/yoke-thrust/charge/hit. All source bodies share181px standing height. Extended charge requires256x192 frame to preserve tail, yoke and outstretched feet; world body scaling remains80px. Ground anchors follow supporting feet, x follows trunk between four legs. No per-frame stretch. Ground review correction: airborne charge feet retain their raised offset above the nominal ground; low weapon cap does not move body grounding.",
